sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User Browser
    participant Gateway as OpenShift Gateway<br/>(Envoy)<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant RBAC as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP TLS
    participant Workbench as Workbench Container<br/>(JupyterLab / Code Server / RStudio)<br/>8888 or 8787/TCP HTTP

    Note over User,Workbench: Flow 1: User Workbench Access
    User->>Gateway: HTTPS/443<br/>TLS 1.2+<br/>OIDC Auth
    Gateway->>RBAC: HTTPS/8443<br/>TLS<br/>Bearer Token
    RBAC->>Workbench: HTTP/8888 or 8787<br/>None (localhost)<br/>Pre-authenticated
    Workbench-->>RBAC: Response (notebook content)
    RBAC-->>Gateway: HTTPS Response
    Gateway-->>User: HTTPS Response

    participant KFP as KFP Pipeline Controller
    participant Runtime as Runtime Container Pod
    participant S3 as External Data Sources<br/>(S3 / Databases)<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    Note over KFP,S3: Flow 2: Pipeline Runtime Execution
    KFP->>Runtime: Create Pod<br/>ServiceAccount auth
    Runtime->>S3: HTTPS/443<br/>TLS 1.2+<br/>AWS IAM / Credentials
    S3-->>Runtime: Data / Model artifacts
    Runtime-->>KFP: Execution result (exit code + artifacts)

    participant GitHub as GitHub PR Event
    participant Tekton as PipelinesAsCode<br/>(Tekton)
    participant Quay as quay.io registry

    Note over GitHub,Quay: Flow 3: Image Build (Konflux)
    GitHub->>Tekton: Webhook<br/>HTTPS/443<br/>TLS 1.2+<br/>GitHub webhook secret
    Tekton->>Tekton: Build multi-arch images<br/>(non-hermetic)
    Tekton->>Quay: Push image<br/>HTTPS/443<br/>TLS 1.2+<br/>Registry credentials
    Tekton->>Quay: Verify (skopeo inspect)<br/>HTTPS/443<br/>Registry credentials
